## 5. Localized URLs

| Page | me (default, no prefix) | en | it | ru | tr |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Home | `/` | `/en` | `/it` | `/ru` | `/tr` |
| Menu | `/meni` | `/en/menu` | `/it/menu` | `/ru/menyu` | `/tr/menu` |
| Menu category | `/meni/dorucak` | `/en/menu/dorucak` | `/it/menu/dorucak` | `/ru/menyu/dorucak` | `/tr/menu/dorucak` |
| Gallery | `/galerija` | `/en/gallery` | `/it/galleria` | `/ru/galereya` | `/tr/galeri` |
| About | `/o-nama` | `/en/about` | `/it/chi-siamo` | `/ru/o-nas` | `/tr/hakkimizda` |
| Contact | `/kontakt` | `/en/contact` | `/it/contatti` | `/ru/kontakty` | `/tr/iletisim` |

- The **folder name in `app/[locale]/` is the internal key** (`meni/`, `o-nama/`, `kontakt/`). Do not rename folders to match translations.
- In code always use the internal key: `<Link href="/meni">`, `getPathname({ locale, href: "/meni" })`, `buildAlternates(locale, "/meni")`. Never hardcode `/en/menu` strings.
- Every new page must also be added to `pathnames` in `i18n/routing.ts` (and to `pages` in `app/sitemap.ts`).
- The QR code always points to `https://restoranharis.com/meni`.
- Category pages are one dynamic route, `"/meni/[category]"` in `pathnames`. The category slug (`dorucak`, `rucak`, `vecera`, `dezerti`, `posni-meni`, from `data/menu/index.ts`) is **the same in every language**, so the language switcher can pass it through unchanged. Link with `href={{ pathname: "/meni/[category]", params: { category: slug } }}`. Translated slugs would need a slug map per language and switcher support; decide before launch, because these become public URLs.
- Verified in dev: `/me/meni` redirects to `/meni`, and a mixed path like `/en/meni` redirects (307) to `/en/menu`.
- The Gallery and About slugs for EN/IT/RU/TR (`gallery`, `galleria`, `galereya`, `galeri`; `about`, `chi-siamo`, `o-nas`, `hakkimizda`) are provisional until a native speaker checks them. Change them only before launch, as they become public URLs.

