## 9. Design system

**Look:** warm, friendly, sweet. Round shapes echo the circular logo. Cream background on every page, maroon as the main color, peach for highlights. Restraint: one memorable element per screen, everything else quiet. The header (a maroon bar with the logo) is the site's strong element; on `/meni` the dark welcome panel is the one memorable element, everything else stays on cream.

### Colors (sampled from the logo)

| Role | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Maroon | `#892E30` | Primary: buttons, prices, active states, links; header bar and mobile menu panel. The logo's exact maroon |
| Peach | `#FFD29F` | Secondary: chips, highlights, section backgrounds; header line and active header link |
| Cream | `#FFF2DC` | Page background (all pages), cards, popovers; text on maroon (header links, buttons). The logo's inner cream `#FFE4B8` mixed half with white |
| Cocoa | `#2E1517` | Body text |

Supporting shades, tuned to stay visible on the cream: `muted` `#F5E2C8` (soft panels), `accent` `#FFE4B8` (menu item hover, the logo's inner cream), `border`/`input` `#E6CBAD`, `secondary-foreground`/`accent-foreground` `#5A1A1E`, `muted-foreground` `#7A5A52`.

Contrast: cocoa on cream 15.4:1, maroon on cream 7.6:1, cream on maroon 7.6:1 (header links, buttons), maroon on peach 6.0:1, peach on maroon 6.0:1 (active header link), `muted-foreground` on cream 5.6:1 and on `muted` 4.9:1, `accent-foreground` on `accent` 10.6:1. **Never put peach text on a light background** (peach on cream is 1.3:1).

Tokens are defined in `app/globals.css` (shadcn variables overridden with the brand values, plus `bg-brand-maroon`, `bg-brand-peach`, `bg-brand-cream`, `bg-brand-cocoa` and the matching `text-`/`border-` classes). Use semantic classes (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) first and brand classes only when needed. No white anywhere: cards and popovers (`--card`, `--popover`) are the same cream. They stand out from the page only through their shadow/ring or border, so keep those when restyling.

### Typography

- Headings: **Lora**, a warm serif (chosen by the client on 2026-10-14, replacing Nunito). `font-heading`, applied to h1 to h4 globally with `tracking-[-0.01em]`; h1/h2 default to `font-bold`, the hero h1 uses `font-semibold`, and links, buttons, language codes and the "Pogledajte meni" cue use `font-semibold`. Weights 400–700 only: never use `font-extrabold`/`font-black` with it.
- Choosing a font: check the letters in the font file itself, not the google/fonts `METADATA.pb` subsets. Alice was the client's first choice, and its metadata lists latin-ext, but it has no č ć š ž đ, ğ or ş. In the browser another font silently drew those letters. Kurale/Gabriela, Bona Nova and Alegreya were the checked alternatives.
- Body: **Inter** (`font-sans`)
- Both must cover `latin`, `latin-ext`, `cyrillic` (č ć š ž đ, ğ ı ş, Russian)
- Line length under about 70 characters. Sentence case. No ALL CAPS eyebrow labels above headings.

**Fonts are self-hosted with `next/font/local`. Do not go back to `next/font/google`.** With Turbopack, Google Fonts sometimes returns `fonts.gstatic.com/l/font?kit=...&skey=...` URLs, which break the build with `Module not found: Can't resolve '@vercel/turbopack-next/internal/font/google/font'` / `next/font/google queries have exactly one entry`. The broken CSS is also saved in `.next/dev`, so the error survives restarts.

**`lib/fonts.ts`**
```ts
import localFont from "next/font/local"

export const lora = localFont({
  src: "../app/fonts/Lora.woff2",
  weight: "400 700",
  variable: "--font-lora",
  display: "swap",
  adjustFontFallback: "Times New Roman",
  declarations: [
    { prop: "ascent-override", value: "100.6%" },
    { prop: "descent-override", value: "27.4%" },
    { prop: "line-gap-override", value: "0%" },
  ],
})

export const inter = localFont({
  src: "../app/fonts/Inter.woff2",
  weight: "100 900",
  variable: "--font-inter",
  display: "swap",
})
```
Both files in `app/fonts/` are variable woff2 fonts from github.com/google/fonts, with their OFL licence files next to them:
- `Lora.woff2` (83 KB) is the **unmodified** `ofl/lora/Lora[wght].ttf` (v3.008, weights 400–700, all of latin-ext and Cyrillic), only compressed to woff2 (with `wawoff2`). **Do not subset it.** Its licence reserves the name "Lora", and a cut-down (modified) font would have to be renamed. The `*-override` declarations copy the font's own hhea metrics, so every OS places the text the same way. Without them Windows uses the font's much taller win metrics and text sits about 1.4px lower in a 16px line.
- `Inter.woff2` (142 KB) is cut down to the latin + latin-ext + cyrillic ranges, all weights 100–900, optical-size axis fixed at 14. Inter's licence reserves no name. To build a file like this, the npm package `subset-font` works (this machine has no Python pip/venv).

In `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`: `<html lang={...} className={cn(lora.variable, inter.variable, ...)}>`. `globals.css` maps `--font-lora` to `--font-heading` (fallbacks Georgia, serif) and `--font-inter` to `--font-sans`. Do not rename the variables to `--font-sans`/`--font-heading`.

### Shape and layout

- Radius: large. Cards `rounded-2xl`/`rounded-3xl`, buttons and chips pill-shaped (`rounded-full`).
- Spacing: 8px grid, sections `py-16 md:py-24`. **One site width: `max-w-7xl px-4`** for the header, the hero, page headings and page content, all pages including the menu (client, 2026-10-14; before, content was `max-w-6xl` and the category page `max-w-2xl`).
