### Language switcher

A **dropdown** (shadcn `DropdownMenu`). The button shows only the current language's code (`ME`, `EN`, ...), no flag, Lora medium `text-sm tracking-wide` on a soft cream rounded square (`h-8 rounded-lg px-2.5 bg-brand-cream/15`, `/25` on hover and while open), as in the client's design (2026-10-14). The list is unchanged. The list shows a flag and code for EN, RU, IT, TR, ME (`switcherLocales`), with a check close to the current one: the list is `w-auto min-w-(--anchor-width)`, so it fits its content instead of the default `min-w-48`. The list uses Lora semibold. Inline pills for every language do not fit on a phone next to the logo.
- Flags: **the official national flags, never simplified, stylised or redrawn (coats of arms included).** The client rejected circle-flags' simplified Montenegro flag as disrespectful. Showing them **round** is wanted, but only as a crop of the real flag (`rounded-full object-cover`), never as a redesigned round flag. Source: Wikimedia Commons (public domain): `Flag_of_Montenegro.svg` (1:2, gold border, full coat of arms), `Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom.svg` (3:5), `Flag_of_Italy.svg`, `Flag_of_Russia.svg`, `Flag_of_Turkey.svg` (2:3).
  - Files in `public/flags/`: `gb.svg`, `it.svg`, `ru.svg`, `tr.svg` as downloaded. `me.png` (192x96) is rendered with sharp from the official SVG, because that SVG is 124 KB (the detailed coat of arms) and the PNG is 6.3 KB. It is 96px tall, so the round crop stays sharp on 3x screens up to 32px (3 x 32 = 96; render it taller if the flags grow).
  - Display: `size-5 rounded-full object-cover`, a 20px circle cropped from the real flag so that **the flag's emblem is in the middle of the circle**. UK, Italy, Russia and Montenegro are symmetric, so they use the plain centre crop (the Montenegro coat of arms measures exactly centred in `me.png`). Turkey's crescent and star sit towards the hoist, so a centre crop cut the crescent: it has `object-[17%_center]` (`flagPosition` in `language-switcher.tsx`; the emblem spans 15000-55318 of the 90000-wide SVG). Any new flag with an off-centre emblem gets its own position the same way. Flags appear only in the list (taken off the button 2026-10-14). No outline ring. `unoptimized`, since they are already right-sized. On Montenegro the whole coat of arms (crown, sceptre, orb) stays inside the circle, with the gold border at top and bottom.
  - Tried and rejected: 28px with a `ring-1 ring-black/10` outline and 32px (the client went back to the original 20px, no ring), the whole uncropped flag inside a circle, and rectangles.
  - Decorative (`alt=""`), because the code and name carry the meaning. **EN uses the UK flag.** Do not use emoji flags: Windows shows them as plain letters. Implementation (`components/layout/language-switcher.tsx`): `useLocale` from next-intl, `usePathname`/`useRouter` from `@/i18n/navigation`, `useParams` from `next/navigation`, a `DropdownMenuRadioGroup`, and `router.replace({ pathname, params }, { locale })` inside `startTransition`. On a dynamic route `usePathname` returns the template (`/meni/[category]`), so the params go along to fill it (next-intl's documented pattern, with a `@ts-expect-error` because TypeScript cannot see that the two match). Notes:
- Base UI radio items do not close the menu by default: each item has `closeOnClick`.
- The code (`ME`, `EN`, ...) is in a span with `-translate-y-[0.5px]`, in the button and in the list. Lora's capitals sit about 0.6px below the middle of their line box, so the code looked lower than the flag and the hamburger next to it (with Nunito it was the reverse, 0.6px higher, and the client noticed). Measured with Lora: within 0.4px of the hamburger at 1x and 0.2px at 2x/3x. A translate is not snapped to whole pixels, so it lands within about 0.15px of the line on 1.7x-3x screens. Tried and dropped: `text-box: trim-both cap alphabetic`, which overshoots by 0.4-0.7px because Chrome puts the trimmed baseline on a whole CSS pixel.
- Screen readers: the button contains a `sr-only` `localeSwitcher.label` before the visible code, so its name is "Izaberite jezik ME". Each item has the code plus a `sr-only` native name ("EN English") and `lang={hreflang[l]}`, so the name is pronounced correctly. Keep the visible code inside the accessible name: do not replace it with an `aria-label`.
- Verified: choosing English on `/meni` goes to `/en/menu`, and on `/meni/rucak` to `/en/menu/rucak`.

