- **`DishCard`** (client, for the photo's load state; no card box since 2026-10-16, user): a row like a printed menu line, separated by a thin `border-primary/15` rule (solid, not dashed: user). A photo box of the same size for every dish (`h-24 w-28`, `sm:h-28 sm:w-36`, `lg:h-32 lg:w-44`) with the photo at its own aspect ratio inside; photos cut out with their background (Posni meni) get `rounded-2xl` + shadow + ring, transparent cut-outs (`transparent: true`) none. Beside it: the name (h3, Lora semibold) with a dotted leader out to the price (Lora bold maroon); on phones no leader, the price goes under the text. Then the ingredients and the flavours (`menu.category.flavors` "Ukusi:" + list), both optional, in Lora like the rest of the card (user, 2026-10-16). Items without a photo are the text alone. A section can have one `image` for all its items (Sladoled), shown beside its h2. A page with one section hides the chip row. While the photo loads, a shadcn `Skeleton` fills the frame. The photo sits on top of it (`relative`), so it shows as soon as it has loaded, even before the page's JS runs, and the skeleton is removed on `onLoad` to stop its pulse (`next/image` also fires `onLoad` for photos that finished before hydration). Only the first section's photos load with the page; the others load (behind skeletons) when their chip is picked. Cards get texts already in the page's language (the page maps `L` to strings, so only one language is sent to the browser).
- Photos: cut out of the client's printed menu, 900px wide and 411-730px tall (1.2:1 salads to 2.2:1 crepes), with the print's background (swirl pattern, beige blocks) baked in. In the cards they fill a **2:1 frame** (`aspect-2/1 object-cover`): the crepes stay nearly whole, salads, pizzas and sandwiches become close-ups of their middle. `tuna-salata.webp` has a thin white strip on its right edge from the cut. `alt=""` because the name is right below.
- **Dish number and "no pork"** (2026-10-19): a dish with a printed `number` (pizzas, salads, crepes, pancakes, waffles) shows it in a small maroon circle before its name, inside the h3; guests order the sweet crepes by it, as their name is the ingredient list. A dish with the printed "NO PORK" badge (`noPork`) gets a shadcn `Badge` (`components/ui/badge.tsx`, added with the CLI) under the ingredients: outline, maroon text, Lora, `menu.category.noPork` "Bez svinjetine".
- Later: small `Badge`s for vegan, new, allergens.
- Allergen note at the bottom, translated.
- Must load fast on mobile data.

**Category photos:** the client's own, one dish per category imported in `data/menu/index.ts` from the category's photo folder (2026-10-19). Budi sam svoj šef has no photos of its own and borrows sweet crepe #22; Slatka karta uses `dezerti/vocni-kup.webp`. The Unsplash placeholders (`public/images/menu/<slug>.jpg`) were deleted, except `vecera.jpg`, still the welcome panel's placeholder (meat with broccoli on a white plate, yoseph hailu, unsplash.com/photos/qT8k4uUOpo4, Unsplash License).

### Motion and accessibility

**One motion style for the whole site**, defined at the top of `app/globals.css`. Use it everywhere and do not invent new timings:
- **Timing:** 200ms with `ease-brand` (`cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`, fast start, soft landing). It is set as Tailwind's default, so every `transition-colors`, `transition-opacity`, `transition` etc. gets it automatically. **Never add `duration-*` or `ease-*` classes.**
- **Popups that open and close** (dropdowns, popovers, selects, dialogs): add `transition-popup`, a fade plus a slight zoom (96% to 100%) from the trigger. It relies on Base UI's `data-starting-style`/`data-ending-style`. The dropdown menu uses it.
- **Sheets/drawers:** fade plus a short slide, with the same default timing (`components/ui/sheet.tsx`).
- **Content that appears** (loaded or swapped in): `animate-fade-in` (opacity only).
- **Cards swapped in as a group** (the dish cards when a category chip is picked): `animate-rise-in`, a fade plus a 4px rise over **700ms** with `ease-brand` (the one exception to the 200ms timing, the user wanted this transition slower), staggered with `animationDelay` (80ms steps, capped at 320ms). Always pair it with `motion-reduce:animate-fade-in`.
- **Hover/active states:** `transition-colors` (as on the header links).
- The generated shadcn components were changed to use this: the `tw-animate-css` classes (`animate-in`, `fade-in-0`, `zoom-in-95`, `duration-100`...) were removed from `dropdown-menu.tsx`, and the fixed durations/easing from `sheet.tsx`. Do the same to every new shadcn component you add.
- **Reduced motion:** `transition-popup` and the sheet fade only (no zoom/slide) when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set. Keep that for anything new (`motion-reduce:transition-opacity`).
- Verified in Chrome: the dropdown fades in and out in about 200ms; the sheet and its overlay use 200ms + `ease-brand`; with reduced motion only opacity transitions.

Still little motion overall: no fade-and-slide on every section, no hover animation on every card. One deliberate moment at most.
- Visible keyboard focus (already set in `globals.css`), alt text on all images, `aria-label`s translated.

