## 11. QR code

Target: **`https://restoranharis.com/meni`**. Static QR, no third-party service, free forever as long as the domain is owned.

**`scripts/generate-qr.ts`**
```ts
import QRCode from 'qrcode';
import { mkdirSync } from 'fs';

const URL = 'https://restoranharis.com/meni';
mkdirSync('qr', { recursive: true });

(async () => {
  await QRCode.toFile('qr/menu-qr.svg', URL, { type: 'svg', errorCorrectionLevel: 'H', margin: 2 });
  await QRCode.toFile('qr/menu-qr.png', URL, { type: 'png', errorCorrectionLevel: 'H', margin: 2, width: 2000 });
  console.log('Done ->', URL);
})();
```

- **SVG for print**, PNG for digital use.
- Print at least 2 x 2 cm, dark on light, keep the white margin.
- Test with an iPhone and an Android phone before printing in bulk.
- Only print after `https://restoranharis.com/meni` is confirmed live over HTTPS.

One-off QR for anything else: `npx qrcode -o code.svg -e H "https://example.com"`

